{
  "configuration_id": "config_047",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_013 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, concat) achieved 0.715 accuracy, far exceeding image-only config_014 (0.332), confirming that multimodal fusion with a learned RNA encoder is the dominant design. The remaining question is whether the simple avgpool aggregation is a bottleneck for combining multiple profiles. This experiment (config_047) isolates that single change—replacing avgpool with transformer aggregation while keeping the proven scvi_n200 encoder, imagenet_vit_l image encoder, and concat fusion—testing whether learned attention across profiles can outperform uniform averaging. Transformer aggregation is the most architecturally impactful untested dimension for a multiprofile model, as it lets the model weight profiles adaptively rather than treating them equally. Expected cost is moderate: transformer attention adds roughly 1–1.5 GPU hours over the 4.49 h baseline, so ~5.5–6 GPU hours. With 7 experiments remaining, this is a high-value exploitation step on the best-known configuration before branching to other axes (RNA encoder, image encoder, fusion)."
}

